From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: register the SFP PHY driver with the 6.18 array API

6.18 removed phy_driver_register() and phy_driver_unregister(); only the
array forms phy_drivers_register()/phy_drivers_unregister() are exported.
sfp_phy.c still calls the single-driver versions:

  src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c:691: error: implicit declaration of function 'phy_driver_register'; did you mean 'phy_drivers_register'?

Register the one sfp_phy_driver through the array form (count 1), which
is exactly what the removed wrapper did.

Classification: portability (kernel API, no behaviour change).

--- a/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c
+++ b/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c
@@ -688,7 +688,7 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 	if(sfp_phy_drv_registered == A_FALSE)
 	{
-		ret = phy_driver_register(&sfp_phy_driver, THIS_MODULE);
+		ret = phy_drivers_register(&sfp_phy_driver, 1, THIS_MODULE);
 		sfp_phy_drv_registered = A_TRUE;
 	}
 	return ret;
@@ -698,7 +698,7 @@
 {
 	if (sfp_phy_drv_registered == A_TRUE)
 	{
-		phy_driver_unregister(&sfp_phy_driver);
+		phy_drivers_unregister(&sfp_phy_driver, 1);
 		sfp_phy_drv_registered = A_FALSE;
 	}
 }
